universal answer to that question is gunpowder. And people say gunpowder because when gunpowder ignites, it expands rapidly, creating tremendous pressure inside the barrel of a gun. And the only way for that pressure to be released is to push the bullet out the end of the barrel. push the bullet out the end of the barrel. So gunpowder isn't the wrong answer to that question, but it is a woefully incomplete answer because anytime a physical object, be it a bullet or an airplane takes flight, there are these two opposing forces at play. There are the forces that propel the object forward, gunpowder or a jet engine, but there are also these forces that oppose progress, namely gravity and wind resistance. The principal obstacle to a bullet is wind resistance,

